# nanopb options for hef.proto
#
# Pattern syntax: "Name type:FT_X" where Name matches message or
# field names ("Msg.field" for a single field, "Msg.*" for all
# fields of a message, "*" for everything).
#
# Strategy:
#   - `*` → all fields default to FT_CALLBACK. This covers the ~69
#     variable-length fields (repeated / bytes / string / map) in
#     hef.proto without enumerating each one. Scalar fields also
#     route through callbacks, which is slower but lets us avoid
#     having to spell out max_size / max_count bounds we don't know
#     for an arbitrary Hailo-compiled model.
#
# hef_parser.c attaches pb_callback_t handlers on just the fields
# we consume today (header.hw_arch, header.timestamp, the list of
# network groups, etc.). nanopb's default no-op callback silently
# drops the rest while still walking the wire format — necessary
# because skipping a length-delimited field requires knowing its
# length, which means the decoder has to read the value to advance.

* type:FT_CALLBACK
